      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "code": { "language": "plaintext", "showLineNumbers": false, "showMiniMap": false },
        "content": "**Dynamic Mapper service has no `/actuator/prometheus` endpoint** — metrics are pushed via OTLP to Grafana Alloy (`otel.instrumentation.micrometer.enabled=true`). The exact Prometheus metric names your Alloy/Mimir pipeline produces for the Timer-based panels below (*Processing Time*, *C8Y Processing Time*) depend on your collector's unit-suffix setting:\n- This dashboard assumes **no unit infix**: `<name>_sum`, `<name>_count`, `<name>_bucket`.\n- If your pipeline adds one, the real names will be `<name>_milliseconds_sum/_count/_bucket` or `<name>_seconds_sum/_count/_bucket`.\n- Open **Explore** on the `$datasource` variable's datasource and search the metrics browser for `dynmapper_inbound_processing_time` to confirm, then edit the affected panel queries.\n\n**CPU Utilization** is not a custom metric emitted by this service's own code (no Spring Boot Actuator / `micrometer-registry-prometheus` dependency exists). It is a best-effort query against `process_runtime_jvm_cpu_utilization`, the standard metric name from the OTel Java runtime-telemetry auto-instrumentation that this service enables (`otel.instrumentation.runtime-telemetry.enabled=true`). Verify the name in your metrics browser and adjust if your collector translates it differently.\n\n**Outbound identity cache hit rate** cannot be shown as a percentage — the code only counts outbound cache *hits* (`dynmapper_outbound_identity_cache_hits_total`); there is no outbound \"total lookups\" counter to divide by (unlike the inbound path). Only the hit rate (count/sec) is shown for outbound.\n\n**C8Y Processing Time** and **Available C8Y Connections** are process-wide (untagged) metrics — the Tenant/Connector selectors do not filter them."
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
